# Copy to .env. Prisma reads this via prisma.config.ts (which imports dotenv).
# A local SQLite file — the library and the commonplace book are one file you own.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# The Rig, from M3. Yours to set by hand — in deployed environments it's a
# Railway environment variable per environment, not committed here.
# `npm run agent:setup` (scripts/setup-agent.ts) creates the Managed Agent
# and its environment (the container workspace every session provisions —
# `sessions.create`'s `environment_id`, needed by app/routes/rig.tsx even
# though the Rig only uses custom tools plus web search/fetch) once each,
# converging both in place on every re-run (skipping the update if nothing
# changed); neither is ever created in the request path. scripts/release.ts
# also runs this on every deploy, when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set for that
# environment. The ids/version themselves live in the RigProvisioning DB
# table, not here — see that model's doc comment in prisma/schema.prisma.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# PostHog browser analytics configuration.
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
